diff --git a/research/reader-w57-pilot/README.md b/research/reader-w57-pilot/README.md
index a4b5816..761d12b 100644
--- a/research/reader-w57-pilot/README.md
+++ b/research/reader-w57-pilot/README.md
@@ -86,3 +86,17 @@ W47 and W51 local screenshots (18 November 2026) show the original behavior:
 the panel control belonged to the right panel and appeared at the top when
 folded and in the panel header when open. W57 is the latest accepted styling
 reference; 'ARGON' is the design prototype name, not the website/Reader brand.
+
+### Canary: native mobile sheet
+
+On a built preview open `/articles/dzhon-gill-chast-2-uchenyi/?reader-pilot=1&reader-layout=native`.
+This opt-in loads annotations into the native Part TOC when the native contract is
+present. It does not load the desktop pilot shell, move Product controls or change
+reader preferences. An unsupported route remains native without an annotations
+entry. The comparison mode is explicit and stays fixed across viewport changes;
+`?reader-pilot=1` without `reader-layout=native` still opens the original witness.
+This is not a mobile-default rollout or an Astro production integration.
+
+From the same checkout, after the production-like build, run the native Chromium
+regression with `node scripts/reader-w57-native-browser-qa.mjs`. An externally
+installed Chromium can be selected with `W57_CHROMIUM_PATH`.
